Feature:

Background: This executes once per feature file
	Given these properties
		|portal.release|true|
		|portal.upstream|true|
		|testray.main.component.name|Portal Instances|

Setup: This executes before each scenario 
	Given TestCase set Up Portal Instance
	When User first Login PG

Teardown: This executes after each scenario 
	Given PortalInstances tear Down CP
		|testPortalInstance|TestPropsUtil#get('test.portal.instance')|
Scenario: Add Portal Instance
Priority: 5
	Given these properties
		|test.name.skip.portal.instance|PortalconfigurationUsecase#AddPortalInstance|
	When ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Virtual Instances|
	And PortalInstances add CP
		|mailDomain|www.able.com|
		|virtualHost|www.able.com|
		|webId|www.able.com|
	Then PortalInstances view CP
		|virtualHost|www.able.com|
Scenario: Default Portal Landing Page
Priority: 5
	Given these properties
		|test.name.skip.portal.instance|PortalconfigurationUsecase#DefaultPortalLandingPage|
	When ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Instance Settings|
	And PortalSettings edit Default Landing Page CP
		|defaultLandingPage|/web/guest/landing|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Sites|
	And TestCase get Site Name
##########################################################
The Poshi return element is not supported in the readable syntax. Please update this test.
##########################################################
		|siteName|${siteName}|
	And Page add
		|pageName|landing|
		|siteName|${siteName}|
	And User logout PG
	And User login PG
		|password|test|
		|userEmailAddress|test@liferay.com|
	And these variables
		|portalURL|TestPropsUtil#get('portal.url')|
	Then AssertLocation the value '${portalURL}/web/guest/landing'
Scenario: Delete Portal Instance
Priority: 5
	Given these properties
		|test.name.skip.portal.instance|PortalconfigurationUsecase#DeletePortalInstance|
	When ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Virtual Instances|
	And PortalInstances add CP
		|mailDomain|www.able.com|
		|virtualHost|www.able.com|
		|webId|www.able.com|
	Then PortalInstances delete CP
		|virtualHost|www.able.com|
Scenario: Permission Check Portal Instances
Priority: 4
	Given these properties
		|test.name.skip.portal.instance|PortalconfigurationUsecase#PermissionCheckPortalInstances|
	When ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Virtual Instances|
	And PortalInstances add CP
		|mailDomain|www.able.com|
		|virtualHost|www.able.com|
		|webId|www.able.com|
	And PortalInstances add CP
		|mailDomain|www.baker.com|
		|virtualHost|www.baker.com|
		|webId|www.baker.com|
	And User first Login PG
		|password|test|
		|userEmailAddress|test@www.able.com|
		|virtualHostsURL|http://www.able.com:8080|
	And Navigator open Specific URL
		|url|http://www.able.com:8080|
	And ProductMenu goto Sites Content
		|portlet|Documents and Media|
	And DMDocument add CP
		|dmDocumentDescription|DM Document Description|
		|dmDocumentFile|Document_1.doc|
		|dmDocumentTitle|DM Document Title|
	And DMNavigator goto Document CP
		|dmDocumentTitle|DM Document Title|
	And DMDocument view CP
		|dmDocumentTitle|DM Document Title|
	And these variables
		|documentURL|selenium#getLocation()|
	And these variables
		|otherInstanceAccessAttempt|StringUtil#replace('${documentURL}', 'able', 'baker')|
	And User first Login PG
		|password|test|
		|userEmailAddress|test@www.baker.com|
		|virtualHostsURL|http://www.baker.com:8080|
	And Navigator open Specific URL
		|url|${otherInstanceAccessAttempt}|
	And Alert view Request Failed To Complete
	Then AssertTextEquals assert Partial Text the value 'You do not have the required permissions.' at locator 'Message#ERROR_2'
Scenario: View Deactivated Portal Instance
Priority: 5
	Given these properties
		|test.name.skip.portal.instance|PortalconfigurationUsecase#ViewDeactivatedPortalInstance|
	When ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|System Settings|
	And Navigator goto Nav Item
		|navItem|Foundation|
	And SystemSettings edit Configuration
		|configurationName|Inactive Request Handler|
	And SystemSettings enable Setting
		|checkboxSetting|SHOW_INACTIVE_REQUEST_MESSAGE|
	And SystemSettings save Configuration
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Virtual Instances|
	And PortalInstances add CP
		|mailDomain|www.able.com|
		|virtualHost|www.able.com|
		|webId|www.able.com|
	And Navigator open URL
	And Page add
		|pageName|Blogs Page|
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Blogs Page|
	And Portlet add PG
		|portletName|Blogs|
	And Page add
		|pageName|Wiki Page|
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Wiki Page|
	And Portlet add PG
		|portletName|Wiki|
	And Page add
		|pageName|Language Page|
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Language Page|
	And Portlet add PG
		|portletName|Language Selector|
	And User logout PG
	And User first Login PG
		|password|test|
		|userEmailAddress|test@www.able.com|
		|virtualHostsURL|http://www.able.com:8080|
	And Page view No PG
		|pageName|Blogs Page|
	And Page view No PG
		|pageName|Wiki Page|
	And Page view No PG
		|pageName|Language Page|
	And Navigator open Specific URL
		|url|http://www.able.com:8080|
	And Page add
		|pageName|Web Content Page|
	And Navigator goto Specific URL Page
		|pageName|Web Content Page|
		|url|http://www.able.com:8080|
	And Portlet add PG
		|portletName|Web Content Display|
	And Navigator goto Specific URL Page
		|pageName|Web Content Page|
		|url|http://www.able.com:8080|
	And Portlet add PG
		|portletName|Hello World|
	And User logout PG
	And User login PG
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Virtual Instances|
	And PortalInstances deactivate Portal Instance
		|virtualHost|www.able.com|
	And Navigator open Specific URL
		|url|http://www.able.com:8080|
	Then Page view Inactive Request Message
		|resource|instance|
Scenario: View Virtual Host Private Site Page
Priority: 4
	Given these properties
		|custom.properties|virtual.hosts.valid.hosts=localhost,127.0.0.1,www.able.com,www.baker.com,www.charlie.com|
	When these properties
		|test.name.skip.portal.instance|PortalconfigurationUsecase#ViewVirtualHostPrivateSitePage|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Instance Settings|
	And PortalSettings edit Virtual Host CP
		|virtualHostName|www.able.com|
	And Navigator open URL
	And ProductMenu goto Sites Configuration
		|portlet|Site Settings|
	And Site add Virtual Hosts URLCP
		|publicPageVirtualHostURL|www.baker.com|
		|publicVirtualHosts|${publicPageVirtualHostURL}|
	And Navigator open URL
	And ProductMenu goto Sites Configuration
		|portlet|Site Settings|
	And Site add Virtual Hosts URLCP
		|privatePageVirtualHostURL|www.charlie.com|
		|privateVirtualHosts|${privatePageVirtualHostURL}|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Sites|
	And Page add
		|pageName|Public Page|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Sites|
	And Page add
		|pageName|Private Page|
		|sitePagePrivacy|Private Pages|
	And Navigator open Specific URL
		|url|http://www.charlie.com:8080|
	And these variables
		|key_pageName|Welcome|
	And AssertElementPresent the value 'Welcome' at locator 'Home#PAGE'
	And User login PG
		|password|test|
		|specificURL|http://www.charlie.com:8080/group/guest|
		|userEmailAddress|test@liferay.com|
	And these variables
		|key_pageName|Private Page|
	And AssertTextEquals the value 'Private Page' at locator 'Home#PAGE'
	And User logout PG
	Then User login User PG
		|password|test|
		|userEmailAddress|test@liferay.com|
Scenario: View Virtual Instance Inherits System Settings
Priority: 4
	Given these properties
		|test.name.skip.portal.instance|PortalconfigurationUsecase#ViewVirtualInstanceInheritsSystemSettings|
	When ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|System Settings|
	And SystemSettings goto Category
		|category|Foundation|
	And SystemSettings edit Configuration
		|configurationName|LDAP Auth|
	And SystemSettings enable Setting
		|checkboxSetting|ENABLED_CHECKBOX|
	And SystemSettings save Configuration
	And Navigator open URL
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Virtual Instances|
	And PortalInstances add CP
		|mailDomain|www.able.com|
		|virtualHost|www.able.com|
		|webId|www.able.com|
	And User first Login PG
		|password|test|
		|userEmailAddress|test@www.able.com|
		|virtualHostsURL|http://www.able.com:8080|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Instance Settings|
	And PortalSettingsNavigator goto LDAP
	Then PortalSettings view Enabled LDAP Setting
		|enableCheckboxKey|ENABLED|